module vawd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Western District of Virginia's own criminal periods. Stated in the
// rules but not declared: the presentence report deemed disclosed one day
// after a verbal announcement that it is available or three days after a
// copy or notice is mailed (Criminal Rule 32(c)), which fixes the trigger
// of FRCrimP 32(f)(1)'s objection period (lit/frcrimp's) rather than a
// period of its own; the government's substantial-assistance motion, due
// with its FRCrimP 32(f) objections (Criminal Rule 32(b)); and the
// appellant's 14 days for a reply on an appeal from a magistrate judge
// (Criminal Rule 59(b)), whose start the rule does not state (a hole).
// The outline's flow (arrest to judgment) is lit/frcrimp's; its decisions
// have no vendored reporter text and are removed.
/// A notice of appeal from a magistrate judge's conviction or sentence is
/// filed under FRCrimP 58(g)(2) (Criminal Rule 59(a)).
event MagistrateAppealNoticed()
/// The transcript of the proceedings before the magistrate judge, which the
/// appellant ordered, is filed (Criminal Rule 59(a)).
event AppealTranscriptFiled()
/// The later of the filing of the appellant's memorandum and the filing of
/// the transcript (Criminal Rule 59(b)).
event AppellantCaseComplete()

/// Criminal Rule 59(a): within 14 days after filing a notice of appeal from
/// a magistrate judge's conviction or sentence, or another period the
/// district judge directs, the appellant files a statement of the grounds
/// for the appeal and a supporting memorandum of law.
deadline appeal-grounds-period: 14.days after MagistrateAppealNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Va. Crim. R. 59(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Criminal Rule 59(a): if the appellant ordered a transcript, the
/// supporting memorandum is filed within 14 days of the filing of the
/// transcript, or another period the district judge directs.
deadline transcript-memorandum-period: 14.days after AppealTranscriptFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Va. Crim. R. 59(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Criminal Rule 59(b): the appellee has 21 days from the filing of the
/// appellant's memorandum or of the transcript, whichever is later, or
/// another period the district judge directs, to file a responsive
/// memorandum.
deadline appeal-response-period: 21.days after AppellantCaseComplete() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Va. Crim. R. 59(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
